course: dictionary
lesson: 15251
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You find the right one by reading the words around it, which are its context. «Many English counties end in -shire, such as Yorkshire.» Here the clue is county, so shire means a large area of a country.
explain: Now read «The Shire horse pulled the heavy cart all day.» A Shire horse is a very large, strong farm horse. The word horse is the clue, so shire is part of a special name here, not a place.
explain: Words can also name a special place in a story. «In the Shire, the hobbits ate big breakfasts and sang songs.» Tolkien's books use a capital S, so the Shire is one special place, not just any county. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence, then try it.
fact: A shire is an old word for a county, a large area of a country.
fact: In England, many counties end in «-shire», such as Yorkshire and Lancashire.
fact: In Australia, a shire is a local council area with its own council.
fact: The Shire is the peaceful home of the hobbits in Tolkien's books.
fact: A Shire horse is a very large, strong farm horse from England. In geography, «the shires» means the countryside of England.
exercise: «Many English counties end in -shire, such as Yorkshire.» What is a shire in this sentence? | A small shop in a village | A type of boat | A kind of tall tree | *A large area of a country, called a county
exercise: «The Shire horse pulled the heavy cart all day.» What kind of animal is a Shire horse? | A wild horse from the hills | *A very large, strong farm horse | A small pet that lives indoors | A fast racing horse from the desert
exercise: «The shire council fixed the bridge near our town.» In Australia, what is a shire? | *A country local council area with its own council | A kind of park for children | A very large farm where horses live | A very old castle
test: «Hobbits lived peacefully in the Shire in Tolkien's books.» What is the Shire? | *The peaceful home of the hobbits | A deep cave under the sea | A school for wizards | A busy city full of shops
test: In geography lessons, «the shires» means which of these? | A type of cake | A city in Scotland | The coast of Australia | *The countryside of England
exam: «Hampshire is a shire in the south of England.» What does shire mean here? | A kind of horse | *A county | A king | A river
